|> Exercise
    handle=_dimensional_f_f_f_

    !! For what kinds of function $f$ (what kinds of
    !! signature) does
    For functions $f$ with what kind of
    signature does the composition
    $$
    \Large f \circ f \circ f
    $$
    make sense?

    |> Solution

        A signature of the form

        $$
        f : [\tA] \ra [\tA]
        $$

        is necessary and sufficient. In more detail,
        the composition

        $$
        f \circ f
        $$

        already requires a signature of this form 
        by Exercise >>_dimensional_f_f_, after which

        $$
        f \circ f : [\tA] \ra [\tA]
        $$

        and

        $$
        f \circ f \circ f = f \circ (f \circ f)
        $$

        is also well-formed, since

        $$
        \begin{gathered}
        f : [\tA] \ra [\tA] \\
        \up{1.6}f \circ f : [\tA] \ra [\tA]
        \end{gathered}
        $$

        can be used in lieu of $f$ and $g$ in a general
        composition $f \circ g$.
